Aerie-Purpose: Tell the Filter Engine which frame and profile a request factory is for, so blocked requests count toward that frame's tab and incognito exceptions stay in their session.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc (WillCreateURLLoaderFactory)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Two more arguments on the call that patch 0001 adds. |frame| is the frame
WillCreateURLLoaderFactory() was given; it is null for workers, which are not
counted. |browser_context| is the profile; an off-the-record one keeps its own
per-site exceptions in memory.

--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -6960,4 +6960,5 @@
   // above, before the network.
-  aerie_adblock::MaybeProxyURLLoaderFactory(type, request_initiator,
-                                            isolation_info, factory_builder);
+  aerie_adblock::MaybeProxyURLLoaderFactory(type, request_initiator,
+                                            isolation_info, factory_builder,
+                                            frame, browser_context);
 
